{"id":"mahabharata-4-012","work":"mahabharata","part":4,"partName":"विराटपर्व","partNameEn":"Virata Parva","unit":12,"title":"द्वादशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 12 · Bhima wrestles Jimuta","summary":{"en":"The Pandavas serve the king and quietly share their earnings. At the great festival of Brahma a mighty wrestler named Jimuta challenges all comers, and at Virata's urging Bhima reluctantly fights and kills him; he is then made to fight lions and elephants for the king's pleasure.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವರು ರಾಜನ ಸೇವೆ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾ ಗಳಿಕೆಯನ್ನು ಮೌನವಾಗಿ ಹಂಚಿಕೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಬ್ರಹ್ಮೋತ್ಸವದಲ್ಲಿ ಜೀಮೂತನೆಂಬ ಮಹಾಮಲ್ಲನು ಎಲ್ಲರಿಗೂ ಸವಾಲು ಹಾಕುತ್ತಾನೆ; ವಿರಾಟನ ಒತ್ತಾಯಕ್ಕೆ ಭೀಮನು ಒಲ್ಲದ ಮನಸ್ಸಿನಿಂದ ಹೋರಾಡಿ ಅವನನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅನಂತರ ರಾಜನ ವಿನೋದಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಸಿಂಹ ಆನೆಗಳೊಂದಿಗೆ ಹೋರಾಡಿಸಲ್ಪಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"पाण्डव राजा की सेवा करते हुए चुपचाप अपनी कमाई बाँटते हैं। ब्रह्मा के महोत्सव में जीमूत नाम का एक महान मल्ल सबको चुनौती देता है, और विराट के आग्रह पर भीम अनिच्छा से लड़कर उसे मार डालते हैं; फिर राजा के मनोरंजन के लिए उन्हें सिंहों और हाथियों से लड़ाया जाता है।","te":"పాండవులు రాజుకు సేవ చేస్తూ సంపాదనను నిశ్శబ్దంగా పంచుకుంటారు. బ్రహ్మోత్సవంలో జీమూతుడనే మహామల్లుడు అందరికీ సవాలు చేస్తాడు; విరాటుని ఒత్తిడితో భీముడు అయిష్టంగా పోరాడి అతనిని చంపుతాడు; తర్వాత రాజు వినోదం కోసం సింహాలు, ఏనుగులతో పోరాడించబడతాడు.","ta":"பாண்டவர்கள் மன்னனுக்குப் பணிபுரிந்தபடி தம் வருவாயை அமைதியாகப் பகிர்ந்துகொள்கிறார்கள். ப்ரஹ்மாவின் பெருவிழாவில் ஜீமூதன் என்ற பெரும் மல்லன் அனைவருக்கும் அறைகூவ, விராடனின் வற்புறுத்தலால் பீமன் விருப்பமின்றிப் போரிட்டு அவனைக் கொல்கிறான்; பின்னர் மன்னனின் பொழுதுபோக்குக்காகச் சிங்கங்களுடனும் யானைகளுடனும் போரிட வைக்கப்படுகிறான்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവർ രാജസേവ ചെയ്യുകയും, സമ്പാദിക്കുന്നത് രഹസ്യമായി പങ്കുവെക്കുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു. ബ്രഹ്മാവിന്റെ മഹോത്സവത്തിൽ ജീമൂതൻ എന്ന ബലവാനായ ഗുസ്തിക്കാരൻ എതിരാളികളെ വെല്ലുവിളിക്കുന്നു. വിരാടന്റെ നിർബന്ധത്താൽ വിമുഖനായ ഭീമൻ അയാളോട് ഏറ്റുമുട്ടി കൊല്ലുന്നു; പിന്നീട് രാജാവിന്റെ വിനോദത്തിനായി സിംഹങ്ങളോടും ആനകളോടും പോരാടേണ്ടിവരുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 4.12; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Dec  1 2011","sections":[{"title":"वैराटपर्व","titleEn":"Vairata Parva (At Virata's court)","verses":[{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवं मत्स्यस्य नगरे वसन्तस्तत्र पाण्डवाः ।\nअत ऊर्ध्वं महावीर्याः किमकुर्वन्त वै द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmin, as the Pandavas lived thus in the Matsya city, what did those mighty heroes do after that?"}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"एवं ते न्यवसंस्तत्र प्रच्छन्नाः कुरुनन्दनाः ।\nआराधयन्तो राजानं यदकुर्वन्त तच्छृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear what the delights of the Kurus did, hidden there and serving the king."}},{"n":3,"text":"युधिष्ठिरः सभास्तारः सभ्यानामभवत्प्रियः ।\nतथैव च विराटस्य सपुत्रस्य विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, as courtier, became dear to the assembly members, and likewise to Virata and his sons, lord of the people."}},{"n":4,"text":"स ह्यक्षहृदयज्ञस्तान्क्रीडयामास पाण्डवः ।\nअक्षवत्यां यथाकामं सूत्रबद्धानिव द्विजान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing the heart of the dice, that Pandava made them play as he wished at the gaming table, like brahmins bound by a string."}},{"n":5,"text":"अज्ञातं च विराटस्य विजित्य वसु धर्मराट् ।\nभ्रातृभ्यः पुरुषव्याघ्रो यथार्हं स्म प्रयच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Winning wealth unknown to Virata, the king of dharma, that tiger among men gave it to his brothers as each deserved."}},{"n":6,"text":"भीमसेनोऽपि मांसानि भक्ष्याणि विविधानि च ।\nअतिसृष्टानि मत्स्येन विक्रीणाति युधिष्ठिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena too sold, for Yudhishthira's sake, the meats and various foods the Matsya king granted him."}},{"n":7,"text":"वासांसि परिजीर्णानि लब्धान्यन्तःपुरेऽर्जुनः ।\nविक्रीणानश्च सर्वेभ्यः पाण्डवेभ्यः प्रयच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna sold the old clothes he received from the women's quarters and gave the money to all the Pandavas."}},{"n":8,"text":"सहदेवोऽपि गोपानां वेषमास्थाय पाण्डवः ।\nदधि क्षीरं घृतं चैव पाण्डवेभ्यः प्रयच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sahadeva too, in a cowherd's dress, gave curds, milk and ghee to the Pandavas."}},{"n":9,"text":"नकुलोऽपि धनं लब्ध्वा कृते कर्मणि वाजिनाम् ।\nतुष्टे तस्मिन्नरपतौ पाण्डवेभ्यः प्रयच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakula also, receiving wealth for his work with the horses when the king was pleased, gave it to the Pandavas."}},{"n":10,"text":"कृष्णापि सर्वान्भ्रातॄंस्तान्निरीक्षन्ती तपस्विनी ।\nयथा पुनरविज्ञाता तथा चरति भामिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the ascetic Krishna, watching over all those brothers, went about so that she should not be recognized again."}},{"n":11,"text":"एवं संपादयन्तस्ते तथान्योन्यं महारथाः ।\nप्रेक्षमाणास्तदा कृष्णामूषुश्छन्ना नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus those great charioteers looked after one another and lived hidden, watching Krishna, O lord of men."}},{"n":12,"text":"अथ मासे चतुर्थे तु ब्रह्मणः सुमहोत्सवः ।\nआसीत्समृद्धो मत्स्येषु पुरुषाणां सुसंमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then in the fourth month a great festival of Brahma, much honored by the people, took place among the Matsyas, grandly."}},{"n":13,"text":"तत्र मल्लाः समापेतुर्दिग्भ्यो राजन्सहस्रशः ।\nमहाकाया महावीर्याः कालखञ्जा इवासुराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wrestlers came from all directions, king, in thousands, huge and mighty, like the Kalakhanja asuras."}},{"n":14,"text":"वीर्योन्नद्धा बलोदग्रा राज्ञा समभिपूजिताः ।\nसिंहस्कन्धकटिग्रीवाः स्ववदाता मनस्विनः ।\nअसकृल्लब्धलक्षास्ते रङ्गे पार्थिवसंनिधौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Swollen with strength and prowess, honored by the king, with lion-like shoulders, waists and necks, bright and proud, they had often won prizes in the arena before kings."}},{"n":15,"text":"तेषामेको महानासीत्सर्वमल्लान्समाह्वयत् ।\nआवल्गमानं तं रङ्गे नोपतिष्ठति कश्चन ॥","meaning":{"en":"One of them, the greatest, challenged all the wrestlers; as he strutted in the arena, no one stood up to him."}},{"n":16,"text":"यदा सर्वे विमनसस्ते मल्ला हतचेतसः ।\nअथ सूदेन तं मल्लं योधयामास मत्स्यराट् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When all the wrestlers were dispirited and disheartened, the Matsya king had his cook fight that wrestler."}},{"n":17,"text":"चोद्यमानस्ततो भीमो दुःखेनैवाकरोन्मतिम् ।\nन हि शक्नोति विवृते प्रत्याख्यातुं नराधिपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Urged on, Bhima set his mind to it unwillingly; for he could not openly refuse the king."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततः स पुरुषव्याघ्रः शार्दूलशिथिलं चरन् ।\nप्रविवेश महारङ्गं विराटमभिहर्षयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that tiger among men, moving like a lazy tiger, entered the great arena, delighting Virata."}},{"n":19,"text":"बबन्ध कक्ष्यां कौन्तेयस्ततस्तं हर्षयञ्जनम् ।\nततस्तं वृत्रसंकाशं भीमो मल्लं समाह्वयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Kunti tied up his girdle, pleasing the crowd, and then Bhima challenged the wrestler, who was like Vritra."}},{"n":20,"text":"तावुभौ सुमहोत्साहावुभौ तीव्रपराक्रमौ ।\nमत्ताविव महाकायौ वारणौ षष्टिहायनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Both were full of great eagerness and fierce valor, like two huge sixty-year-old rutting elephants."}},{"n":21,"text":"चकर्ष दोर्भ्यामुत्पाट्य भीमो मल्लममित्रहा ।\nविनदन्तमभिक्रोशञ्शार्दूल इव वारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima, slayer of enemies, seized the wrestler in his arms, lifted him and dragged him along as he bellowed and cried, as a tiger drags an elephant."}},{"n":22,"text":"तमुद्यम्य महाबाहुर्भ्रामयामास वीर्यवान् ।\nततो मल्लाश्च मत्स्याश्च विस्मयं चक्रिरे परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty-armed hero lifted him and whirled him, and the wrestlers and the Matsyas were greatly astonished."}},{"n":23,"text":"भ्रामयित्वा शतगुणं गतसत्त्वमचेतनम् ।\nप्रत्यपिंषन्महाबाहुर्मल्लं भुवि वृकोदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whirling him a hundred times until he was senseless and lifeless, Vrikodara ground the wrestler into the ground."}},{"n":24,"text":"तस्मिन्विनिहते मल्ले जीमूते लोकविश्रुते ।\nविराटः परमं हर्षमगच्छद्बान्धवैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the world-famous wrestler Jimuta was killed, Virata was overjoyed together with his kinsmen."}},{"n":25,"text":"संहर्षात्प्रददौ वित्तं बहु राजा महामनाः ।\nबल्लवाय महारङ्गे यथा वैश्रवणस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great-minded king in his joy gave Ballava much wealth in that great arena, like Vaishravana."}},{"n":26,"text":"एवं स सुबहून्मल्लान्पुरुषांश्च महाबलान् ।\nविनिघ्नन्मत्स्यराजस्य प्रीतिमावहदुत्तमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus, defeating very many wrestlers and strong men, he brought the Matsya king the highest delight."}},{"n":27,"text":"यदास्य तुल्यः पुरुषो न कश्चित्तत्र विद्यते ।\nततो व्याघ्रैश्च सिंहैश्च द्विरदैश्चाप्ययोधयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When no man there was his equal, the king made him fight with tigers, lions and elephants."}},{"n":28,"text":"पुनरन्तःपुरगतः स्त्रीणां मध्ये वृकोदरः ।\nयोध्यते स्म विराटेन सिंहैर्मत्तैर्महाबलैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And again, inside the palace among the women, Vrikodara was made by Virata to fight with mighty, maddened lions."}},{"n":29,"text":"बीभत्सुरपि गीतेन सुनृत्तेन च पाण्डवः ।\nविराटं तोषयामास सर्वाश्चान्तःपुरस्त्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bibhatsu the Pandava also pleased Virata and all the women of the inner quarters with song and fine dancing."}},{"n":30,"text":"अश्वैर्विनीतैर्जवनैस्तत्र तत्र समागतैः ।\nतोषयामास नकुलो राजानं राजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakula pleased the king with trained, swift horses brought together there from various places, best of kings."}},{"n":31,"text":"तस्मै प्रदेयं प्रायच्छत्प्रीतो राजा धनं बहु ।\nविनीतान्वृषभान्दृष्ट्वा सहदेवस्य चाभिभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"The pleased king gave him much wealth as a reward; and seeing Sahadeva's trained bulls, lord, he did likewise."}},{"n":32,"text":"एवं ते न्यवसंस्तत्र प्रच्छन्नाः पुरुषर्षभाः ।\nकर्माणि तस्य कुर्वाणा विराटनृपतेस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus those bulls among men lived there in disguise, doing the work of King Virata."}}]}]}